    <statement><p>Find the equation for a linear function <m>f(x,y)</m>
with the values given in the table below:</p>
<tabular bottom="medium" left="medium" right="medium" top="medium">
<row>
<cell><m>x\backslash y</m></cell>
<cell><m>-1</m></cell>
<cell>0</cell>
<cell>1</cell>
<cell>2</cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>0</cell>
<cell>-3.5</cell>
<cell>-3</cell>
<cell>-2.5</cell>
<cell>-2</cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>1</cell>
<cell>-2.5</cell>
<cell>-2</cell>
<cell>-1.5</cell>
<cell>-1</cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>2</cell>
<cell>-1.5</cell>
<cell>-1</cell>
<cell>-0.5</cell>
<cell>0</cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell>3</cell>
<cell>-0.5</cell>
<cell>0</cell>
<cell>0.5</cell>
<cell>1</cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p><m>f(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1x+0.5y+-3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x</m> increases by 1,
<m>f(x,y)</m> increases by <m>1</m>, so the <m>x</m> slope is <m>1</m>.
For each row in the table, we find that as <m>y</m> increases by 1,
<m>f(x,y)</m> increases by <m>0.5</m>, so the <m>y</m> slope is <m>0.5</m>.
So the function has the form
<m>f(x,y) = x  + 0.5 y + c</m>.
Also note that <m>f(0,0)=-3</m>, so <m>c=-3</m>. Therefore,
the function is <m>f(x,y) = 1x+0.5y+\left(-3\right)</m>.



</solution>
